# IronLogic AI - Custom Rules & Standards

## 🎯 Tech Stack Preferences
- **Frontend:** Angular 21+, Tailwind CSS, Angular Signals (Avoid RxJS for simple state).
- **Backend:** .NET 10, C# 13 (Use Primary Constructors), Entity Framework Core 10.
- **Architecture:** Clean Architecture (Domain, Application, Infrastructure, API).

## 🛠️ Development Rules
- **Naming:** Use PascalCase for C# and camelCase for TypeScript/JSON.
- **Signals:** Always use Angular Signals for state management in new components.
- **Consistency:** Ensure UI components match the aesthetics of `app-metric-card`.
- **Financials:** Always use `decimal(18,2)` for money-related fields in C#.

## 🧠 Business Logic Constraints
- **Exercises:** Any user-created exercise must default to `Status = Pending` and `IsPublic = false`.
- **Visibility:** Private exercises are only visible to the `CreatorUserId`.
- **Admin Flow:** Only admins can toggle `IsPublic` to true after review.

## 📝 Code Generation Instructions
- Always check `src/app/core/models` before creating new DTOs to ensure alignment.
- When generating Backend code, ensure it supports the "Live Logger" logic in the Athlete Portal.

- **C# Standards:** Always use File-scoped namespaces.
- **Dependency Injection:** Use Primary Constructors (C# 12/13) for Injecting Services into Controllers and Repositories.
- **EF Core:** Follow the 'Code First' approach and ensure all Entities have a dedicated Configuration class (IEntityTypeConfiguration).